<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Welcome to Part 4: Dynamic Explicit Crush Execution, Energy Balance Verification, and Specific Energy Absorption (SEA) Extraction.

2
00:09.000 --> 00:24.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Create a Dynamic Explicit Step named "Crush-Step" with a time period of 0.005 seconds. Enable Improved dt Method to optimize the stable time increment.

3
00:24.000 --> 00:38.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>We apply kinematic boundary conditions: fix all degrees of freedom at the bottom polygonal ring, and prescribe a downward crushing velocity v = 10.0 m/s at the top reference point.

4
00:38.000 --> 00:54.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Request History Outputs for whole-model energy components: ALLIE (total internal energy), ALLKE (kinetic energy), ALLAE (artificial strain energy), and reaction force RF2.

5
00:54.000 --> 01:10.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Post-processing verification: Plot ALLKE versus ALLIE. In a valid quasi-static crash analysis, kinetic energy must stay strictly below 5% of internal energy throughout the entire stroke.

6
01:10.000 --> 01:28.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Finally, extract reaction force vs displacement. Integrate the curve using the trapezoidal rule to calculate Specific Energy Absorption: SEA = integral(F d_delta) divided by total mass.

7
01:28.000 --> 01:42.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>This concludes the 4-part Strut Antiprism masterclass. Review the automated Python script in the laboratory repository to reproduce and optimize your multi-cell designs.
